.TH TUNED-ADM 8 "July 2026" "tuned-rs 0.1.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
tuned-adm \- manage the TuneD-compatible system tuning daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tuned-adm
.RI [ options ]
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tuned-adm
controls the service that owns
.B com.redhat.tuned
on the system D-Bus.  Its command names, output conventions, and exit status
follow the TuneD administration client.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list [profiles|plugins] [--verbose]
List available profiles or runtime plugins.  Profile listing also prints the
active profile.
.TP
.B active
Print the current active profile.
.TP
.B off
Disable active tuning and restore recorded values.
.TP
.B profile [profile ...]
Apply one profile or a stack of profiles in the specified order.  Without a
profile, list available profiles.
.TP
.B profile_info [profile]
Print the selected profile's name, summary, and description.  The active
profile is used when no name is given.
.TP
.B recommend
Print the recommended profile.
.TP
.B verify [--ignore-missing]
Verify the current system state against the active profile.
.TP
.B auto_profile
Enable automatic selection and apply the recommended profile.
.TP
.B profile_mode
Print whether profile selection is manual or automatic.
.TP
.B instance_acquire_devices devices instance
Move matching devices to a dynamic plugin instance.
.TP
.B get_instances [plugin]
List active dynamic instances, optionally restricted by plugin.
.TP
.B instance_get_devices instance
List devices assigned to an instance.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Print command usage.
.TP
.BR -v , " --version"
Print the client version when used before the command.
.TP
.BR -d , " --debug"
Accept the TuneD debug option.
.TP
.BR -a , " --async"
Accept the TuneD asynchronous-operation option.
.TP
.BR -t , " --timeout " seconds
Validate and accept a positive operation timeout.
.TP
.BR -l , " --loglevel " level
Accept the TuneD log-capture level option.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success, one indicates that the requested operation failed or
its arguments were invalid, and three indicates a D-Bus or internal failure.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/tuned/active_profile
Persisted profile selection.
.TP
.I /etc/tuned/profile_mode
Manual or automatic selection mode.
.TP
.I /var/log/tuned/tuned.log
Conventional TuneD log location reported by verification output.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tuned (8),
.BR systemctl (1)
